  "displayField" : "PARK_NAME", 
  "description" : "\u003cDIV STYLE=\"text-align:Left;\"\u003e\u003cDIV\u003e\u003cDIV\u003e\u003cP\u003e\u003cSPAN\u003eSelected, main entrance points for 282 pubicly accessible Units and Properties of the California State Park System, prepared by the California Department of Parks and Recreation (DPR, aka California State Parks, CSP) enterprise GIS team for the purpose of data sharing with cooperating agencies. Attributes include Park name, location, web page link, and direct links to Park Brochure Maps and Campground Maps. DPR recommends internal use only, due to included DPR Administrative Unit coding: Districts, Sectors, Units, plus the foreign key, RECNO, to the DPR GeoFile now superseded by a computer-assisted dispatch CAD system under Agreement with the California Highway Patrol), Contacts: kelly.thorn@parks.ca.gov (Web); victoria.yturralde@parks.ca.gov (Publications, Brochure Maps); Michael Lynch (Communication Centers); gary.walter@parks.ca.gov (enterprise GIS architecture); isaac.oshima@parks.ca.gov (Applications); alan.kilgore@parks.ca.gov (Analysis); paul.veisze@parks.ca.gov (metadata author, GIS Manager; 916-949-3327; DPR Facilities Management Division, 704 O Street, Sacramento, CA 95814; draft 2013.12.11; 2014.06.05; 2015.11.09).\u003c/SPAN\u003e\u003c/P\u003e\u003c/DIV\u003e\u003c/DIV\u003e\u003c/DIV\u003e", 
